or who wants to promote his divisive book and agenda on \"Murphy in the Morning.\" Also, Avery moderates a lively political discussion on his show with locals in Buffalo, N.Y.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/172/430228.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":5,"t":"The Girl Who Cried About Wolf","a":"2018-10-25","l":30,"d":"Fearful of being scooped while legal vets her weighty investigative story, Murphy is exasperated when she learns Frank is dating an anchor, Christy Shepherd, from the competing Wolf Network.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/172/432084.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":6,"t":"Results May Vary","a":"2018-11-01","l":30,"d":"The \"Murphy in the Morning\" team gears up for their live all-day coverage of the mid-term elections, competing against Avery, who is reporting with John Haggerty, the Wolf Network's conservative superstar. Also, Pat is horrified when Miles forces him to wear a conservative suit after assigning him to analyze numbers and trends on-air throughout the day","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/173/433925.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":7,"t":"A Lifetime of Achievement","a":"2018-11-08","l":30,"d":"The \"Murphy in the Morning\" team, Avery and Phyllis join Jim Dial at an eventful lifetime achievement award gala in his honor, hosted by Katie Couric and attended by Murphy's worst-ever secretary, who has a surprising new connection to Murphy. Also, Murphy discovers a kindred spirit in Judge Nate Campbell, another gala attendee.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/174/435625.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":8,"t":"The Coma and the Oxford Comma","a":"2018-11-15","l":30,"d":"The \"Murphy in the Morning\" team strives to land a revealing first interview with Corky's beauty pageant friend, Holly, who just woke up from a 10-year coma that made national headlines.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/174/437240.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":9,"t":"Thanksgiving and Taking","a":"2018-11-22","l":30,"d":"When the culinarily challenged Murphy invites her colleagues plus Phyllis, Miguel and his parents for Thanksgiving dinner with Avery and her, they all brace themselves for the worst.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/175/438725.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":10,"t":"Beat the Press","a":"2018-11-29","l":30,"d":"After Frank is physically attacked while covering a political rally, for the first time in her career Murphy is afraid to dispute the opposing viewpoint of a guest on her show.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/176/440324.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":11,"t":"The Wheels on the Dog Go Round and Round","a":"2018-12-06","l":30,"d":"During Corky's live \"National Adopt a Pet Day\" segment, she guilts Murphy into adopting a dog. Also, Avery's show is moved to the Wolf Network's plum 10:00 PM timeslot, and Phyllis and Miguel get a surprise visit from Fred Noonan, an intimidating health inspector.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/176/441626.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":12,"t":"AWOL","a":"2018-12-13","l":30,"d":"A disillusioned Avery seeks career inspiration from his extended family at \"Murphy in the Morning,\" as the team tries to salvage a major story that hinges on a source in the Middle East who has gone silent.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/177/443059.jpg"},{"s":11,"e":13,"t":"Happy New Year","a":"2018-12-20","l":30,"d":"The gang tries to distract Murphy from worrying about Avery's assignment in Kabul by getting her to attend the special 100th anniversary New Year's Eve celebration at Phil's Bar.","img":"https://static.tvmaze.com/uploads/images/original_untouched/177/444963.jpg"}]}